{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC2 — arm64 / AMI compatibility PROVEN against the AWS API (not inferred from the type name)\n\n```\n$ aws ec2 describe-instance-types --instance-types r7g.large t4g.large\n  r7g.large   arch [arm64]   2 vCPU   16384 MiB   hypervisor nitro   boot [uefi]\n  t4g.large   arch [arm64]   2 vCPU    8192 MiB   hypervisor nitro   boot [uefi]\n\n$ aws ec2 describe-instance-type-offerings --location-type availability-zone \\\n    --filters Name=instance-type,Values=r7g.large Name=location,Values=us-east-1a\n  [\"us-east-1a\"]\n\n$ aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids i-00880b2c7f13527c5\n  AZ us-east-1a   type t4g.large   state running   ami ami-0dc9c39dfb2c22a1e\n\n$ aws ec2 describe-images --image-ids ami-0dc9c39dfb2c22a1e\n  Architecture arm64   BootMode uefi\n  Name al2023-ami-2023.12.20260629.0-kernel-6.1-arm64\n\n$ aws ssm get-parameter --name /aws/service/ami-amazon-linux-latest/al2023-ami-kernel-default-arm64\n  ami-07987a01dcdb011ef      (the parameter main.tf:12-14 resolves; arm64 by parameter name)\n```\n\n**Verdict: compatible.** r7g.large and t4g.large are identical on every attribute the AMI\nconstrains — `arm64`, `nitro`, `uefi` boot mode. The AMI actually attached to the running\ninstance (`ami-0dc9c39dfb2c22a1e`) is an arm64 AL2023 image, and the AMI is pinned by\n`lifecycle { ignore_changes = [ami] }` (`main.tf:96-98`) so the resize does not disturb it.\nThe change is architecture-preserving; there is no unbootable-instance risk from this axis.\n\nThe two types differ ONLY in memory (8192 -> 16384 MiB) and family characteristics: r7g is\nGraviton3 and **not burstable**, t4g is Graviton2 and burstable. vCPU is unchanged at 2, by\ndesign (see the plan).\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788669564005625329,"uuid":"ade4bc85-5e46-47ef-9d6e-39fc1d49a3af"}